  {
    "knowledge_point": {
      "db_id": 17592186204089,
      "id": "d6226fdb-ee73-5a78-87d5-9d6a988a9eb4",
      "title": "Identifying an Equation With No Solutions"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "1a24b052-36b2-52d9-8398-6697e95e63fb",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "Which of the following equations has no solutions?\n\nSelect all that apply.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Let's attempt to solve each equation in turn:\n\n- For the first equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2u-2 & =2u-3 \\\\ 2u-2-2u & =2u-3-2u \\\\ -2 & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis equation is false for all values of $u.$ Therefore, the equation $2u-2=2u-3$ has no solutions.\n\n- For the second equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7u+6 & =7u-4 \\\\ 7u+6-7u & =7u-4-7u \\\\ 6 & =-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis equation is false for all values of $u.$ Therefore, the equation $7u+6=7u-4$ has no solutions.\n\n- For the third equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8u & =7u-1 \\\\ 8u-7u & =7u-1-7u \\\\ u & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation $8u=7u-1$ has the unique solution $u=-1.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $2u-2=2u-3$; $7u+6=7u-4$ only.",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "9456a8ea-8986-5343-b785-dab736f7d546",
          ":answer-field/key": "$2u-2=2u-3$",
