    "question": {
      ":question/id": "01ab1202-8c4d-5032-a8e7-f02d8b651913",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "Which of the following equations has no solutions?\n\nI. $7w-8=7w$\n\nII. $-8w=-8w$\n\nIII. $5w-6=5w-5$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Let's attempt to solve each equation in turn:\n\n- For the first equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7w-8 & =7w \\\\ 7w-8-7w & =7w-7w \\\\ -8 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis equation is false for all values of $w.$ Therefore, the equation $7w-8=7w$ has no solutions.\n\n- For the second equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-8w & =-8w \\\\ -8w+8w & =-8w+8w \\\\ 0 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis equation is true for all values of $w.$\n\n- For the third equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5w-6 & =5w-5 \\\\ 5w-6-5w & =5w-5-5w \\\\ -6 & =-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis equation is false for all values of $w.$ Therefore, the equation $5w-6=5w-5$ has no solutions.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "602f08b8-341b-5ec3-886a-9a1070b21e34",
          ":answer-field/key": "selection",
