    "question": {
      ":question/id": "01b72187-812a-5fcc-9b91-b8d1d00a6595",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "Which of the following equations has no solutions?\n\nSelect all that apply.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Let's attempt to solve each equation in turn:\n\n- For the first equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9z-4 & =9z-4 \\\\ 9z-4-9z & =9z-4-9z \\\\ -4 & =-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis equation is true for all values of $z.$\n\n- For the second equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2z-5 & =8z+4 \\\\ -2z-5-8z+5 & =8z+4-8z+5 \\\\ -10z & =9 \\\\ z & =- \\frac{9}{10}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation $-2z-5=8z+4$ has the unique solution $z=- \\frac{9}{10}.$\n\n- For the third equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3z-3 & =-3z-5 \\\\ -3z-3+3z & =-3z-5+3z \\\\ -3 & =-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis equation is false for all values of $z.$ Therefore, the equation $-3z-3=-3z-5$ has no solutions.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $-3z-3=-3z-5$ only.",
