    "question": {
      ":question/id": "1a894a7e-c367-522f-8adb-1cb37a1e6207",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "Which of the following equations has no solutions?\n\nSelect all that apply.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Let's attempt to solve each equation in turn:\n\n- For the first equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-7y+7 & =-7y+2 \\\\ -7y+7+7y & =-7y+2+7y \\\\ 7 & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis equation is false for all values of $y.$ Therefore, the equation $-7y+7=-7y+2$ has no solutions.\n\n- For the second equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4y+4 & =4y-9 \\\\ 4y+4-4y & =4y-9-4y \\\\ 4 & =-9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis equation is false for all values of $y.$ Therefore, the equation $4y+4=4y-9$ has no solutions.\n\n- For the third equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-8y-6 & =8y-2 \\\\ -8y-6-8y+6 & =8y-2-8y+6 \\\\ -16y & =4 \\\\ y & =- \\frac{1}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation $-8y-6=8y-2$ has the unique solution $y=- \\frac{1}{4}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $-7y+7=-7y+2$; $4y+4=4y-9$ only.",
