    "question": {
      ":question/id": "2d5c4aa7-580d-5a76-8fd1-58728e658a4e",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "Which of the following equations has no solutions?\n\nSelect all that apply.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Let's attempt to solve each equation in turn:\n\n- For the first equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4v-5 & =-8v-5 \\\\ 4v-5+8v+5 & =-8v-5+8v+5 \\\\ 12v & =0 \\\\ v & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation $4v-5=-8v-5$ has the unique solution $v=0.$\n\n- For the second equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-6v+8 & =-6v+8 \\\\ -6v+8+6v & =-6v+8+6v \\\\ 8 & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis equation is true for all values of $v.$\n\n- For the third equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2v-5 & =-2v-4 \\\\ -2v-5+2v & =-2v-4+2v \\\\ -5 & =-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis equation is false for all values of $v.$ Therefore, the equation $-2v-5=-2v-4$ has no solutions.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $-2v-5=-2v-4$ only.",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
