    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "5dd489f2-d06a-55bf-8ce3-3fba5d025409",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "Which of the following equations has no solutions?\n\nSelect all that apply.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Let's attempt to solve each equation in turn:\n\n- For the first equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}w-2 & =w+7 \\\\ w-2-w & =w+7-w \\\\ -2 & =7.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis equation is false for all values of $w.$ Therefore, the equation $w-2=w+7$ has no solutions.\n\n- For the second equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-9w-8 & =-9w-8 \\\\ -9w-8+9w & =-9w-8+9w \\\\ -8 & =-8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis equation is true for all values of $w.$\n\n- For the third equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-6w+1 & =4w-8 \\\\ -6w+1-4w-1 & =4w-8-4w-1 \\\\ -10w & =-9 \\\\ w & =\\frac{9}{10}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation $-6w+1=4w-8$ has the unique solution $w=\\frac{9}{10}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $w-2=w+7$ only.",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "a64ae27d-27db-5134-9740-966217db8226",
