    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "aaf9dc21-9884-5fff-8140-77b0cea25264",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "Which of the following equations has no solutions?\n\nSelect all that apply.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Let's attempt to solve each equation in turn:\n\n- For the first equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3u+5 & =3u+5 \\\\ 3u+5-3u & =3u+5-3u \\\\ 5 & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis equation is true for all values of $u.$\n\n- For the second equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8u-6 & =8u+6 \\\\ 8u-6-8u & =8u+6-8u \\\\ -6 & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis equation is false for all values of $u.$ Therefore, the equation $8u-6=8u+6$ has no solutions.\n\n- For the third equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u+3 & =6u+5 \\\\ u+3-6u-3 & =6u+5-6u-3 \\\\ -5u & =2 \\\\ u & =- \\frac{2}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation $u+3=6u+5$ has the unique solution $u=- \\frac{2}{5}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $8u-6=8u+6$ only.",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "f6513c37-c2ca-5dae-8a72-ac5dbecbfd2c",
          ":answer-field/key": "$3u+5=3u+5$",
