    "question": {
      ":question/id": "7134e12d-6c5e-5c26-a55f-6683f6645d4a",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "Which of the following equations has no solutions?\n\nSelect all that apply.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Let's attempt to solve each equation in turn:\n\n- For the first equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-9y-3 & =-9y-1 \\\\ -9y-3+9y & =-9y-1+9y \\\\ -3 & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis equation is false for all values of $y.$ Therefore, the equation $-9y-3=-9y-1$ has no solutions.\n\n- For the second equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4y+9 & =4y-9 \\\\ 4y+9-4y & =4y-9-4y \\\\ 9 & =-9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis equation is false for all values of $y.$ Therefore, the equation $4y+9=4y-9$ has no solutions.\n\n- For the third equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3y+2 & =-4y-9 \\\\ -3y+2+4y-2 & =-4y-9+4y-2 \\\\ y & =-11.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation $-3y+2=-4y-9$ has the unique solution $y=-11.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $-9y-3=-9y-1$; $4y+9=4y-9$ only.",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "a03926fb-dfdb-5d17-8c13-3a5d35eba9de",
